    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s12",
   "date": "2025-12-10",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251210.pdf",
   "text": "To another degree, it is that AI—spending on data centers and related to AI has been holding up business investment.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
    "speaker_identity_source_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/bios/board/powell.htm",
    "speaker_alias_verified_on": "2026-11-11"
   },
   "analysis": {
    "status": "pending",
    "a": {},
    "b": {},
    "topics": [],
    "confidence": {},
    "escalated": [],
    "models": {},
    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s13",
   "date": "2025-12-10",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251210.pdf",
   "text": "Fiscal policy is going to be supportive. And, as I mentioned, AI spending will continue. The consumer continues to spend.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
    "speaker_identity_source_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/bios/board/powell.htm",
    "speaker_alias_verified_on": "2026-11-11"
   },
   "analysis": {
    "status": "pending",
    "a": {},
    "b": {},
    "topics": [],
    "confidence": {},
    "escalated": [],
    "models": {},
    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s14",
   "date": "2025-12-10",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251210.pdf",
   "text": "So it is—the implication is obviously higher productivity. And some of that may be AI.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
    "speaker_identity_source_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/bios/board/powell.htm",
    "speaker_alias_verified_on": "2026-11-11"
   },
   "analysis": {
    "status": "pending",
    "a": {},
    "b": {},
    "topics": [],
    "confidence": {},
    "escalated": [],
    "models": {},
    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s15",
   "date": "2025-12-10",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251210.pdf",
   "text": "So it’s probably part of the story. It’s not a big part of the story yet. We don’t know whether it will be. But, you know, for example, if you look at—you can’t miss the big announcements of layoffs and also companies saying that they’re not going to hire anybody for a long time, and they cite AI—that’s all clearly happening.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
    "speaker_identity_source_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/bios/board/powell.htm",
    "speaker_alias_verified_on": "2026-11-11"
   },
   "analysis": {
    "status": "pending",
    "a": {},
    "b": {},
    "topics": [],
    "confidence": {},
    "escalated": [],
    "models": {},
    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s16",
   "date": "2025-12-10",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251210.pdf",
   "text": "But, yes, I think we are seeing—we’re definitely seeing higher productivity. I don’t—I think it’s a little quick to be saying it’s generative AI. But I don’t know—you know, the pandemic may have induced people to do more automation and do more things with computers to replace people. And that raises productivity, you know, output per hour.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
    "speaker_identity_source_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/bios/board/powell.htm",
    "speaker_alias_verified_on": "2026-11-11"
   },
   "analysis": {
    "status": "pending",
    "a": {},
    "b": {},
    "topics": [],
    "confidence": {},
    "escalated": [],
    "models": {},
    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s17",
   "date": "2025-10-29",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251029.pdf",
   "text": "And big U.S. companies are just investing a lot of resources in thinking about how AI, which will be based on those data centers, run through data centers, is going to affect their businesses. So it’s a big deal. I don’t think that the spending that happens to build data centers all over the country is especially interest sensitive.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
    "speaker_identity_source_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/bios/board/powell.htm",
    "speaker_alias_verified_on": "2026-11-11"
   },
   "analysis": {
    "status": "pending",
    "a": {},
    "b": {},
    "topics": [],
    "confidence": {},
    "escalated": [],
    "models": {},
    "assessments": {}
   }
  },
  {
   "sid": "s18",
   "date": "2025-10-29",
   "url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20251029.pdf",
   "text": "This is—this is different in the sense that these companies—the companies that are so highly valued—actually have earnings and stuff like that. So you go back to the ’90s and the dot-com [period], they were—these were ideas rather than companies. And we’re—so there’s a clear bubble there, whereas the—I won’t go into particular names, but they actually have earnings, and it looks like they have business models and profits and that kind of thing. So it’s really a different thing. You know, the investment we’re getting in equipment and all those things that go into creating data centers and feeding the AI, it’s clearly one of the big sources of growth in the economy. Consumer spending also, though, has been—is much bigger than that and has been growing and has defied a lot of, you know, negative forecasts, continuing to do so this year.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Jerome H. Powell",
    "organization_id": "federal_reserve",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Automated extraction; exact quote and attribution span matched the retrieved source.",
    "speaker_label": "CHAIR POWELL.",
